/bin/
*.log
.DS_Store
/coverage.out

# Default BLOB_STORAGE_ROOT (ADR-0024) when the env var isn't set — a
# developer running `go run ./cmd/universal-core` from the repo root and
# uploading an attachment would otherwise land real user-supplied file
# content as untracked files in a public repo's working tree (the same
# class of near-miss the seed-demo-data binary note below already
# documents; found by independent review, uc-infra#142).
/data/

# This repo is public. docs/ (ADRs, code-review records) and infra/
# (Terraform) live in the private universaltill/uc-infra repo instead —
# ignored here so an accidental `git add -A` can never re-introduce them.
/docs/
/infra/

# Locally-built cmd binaries (go build ./cmd/... in the repo root) — a
# 13 MB seed-demo-data binary was one git add -A away from the public
# history once (independent review, 2026-07-31). A 15.8 MB
# sync-tenant-modules binary actually landed (uc-infra#184) — this list
# had an entry for every other cmd/ binary except that one.
# internal/repohygiene/gitignore_test.go now guards this list against
# missing an entry the same way again; keep this block's entries in sync
# with cmd/*'s actual directory names or that test fails the build.
/seed-demo-data
/provision-tenant
/migrate
/universal-core
/backfill-purchase-order-status
/backfill-quote-line-unit-price
/backfill-purchase-order-total
/backfill-poline-money
/sync-tenant-modules
/install-module
/backfill-goods-receipt-facility
/backfill-inventory-facility
/backfill-fixedasset-posted-period-count
/backfill-status-name-i18n
/backfill-status-name-translations

# A TestCaptureHelpScreenshots run (internal/e2e/help_screenshot_capture_
# test.go, uc-infra#145) killed mid-write leaves its temp file behind —
# writeAssetAtomic renames it into place on success, so one surviving
# here means an interrupted capture, never a real screenshot `git add -A`
# should pick up.
/internal/help/content/assets/**/.tmp-capture-*

# Isolated worktrees created by Agent(isolation:"worktree") for
# independent-review subagents — a local tooling artifact, never
# something to commit (uc-infra#179's review left one of these behind).
/.claude/worktrees/
